    {
     "head": "How each cell suits its function",
     "text": "A specialised cell has features that suit its function. A root hair cell has a long, thin extension, so it has a large surface area for the uptake of water and mineral ions (8.2). You learn the features of sperm and egg cells in 16.4."
    },
    {
     "ext": true,
     "near": 9,
     "text": "A neurone has long fibres, so an impulse travels a long distance along one cell."
    }
